      "path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp54-entry-eligibility-level-adjustment-and-clauses.md",
      "published_document_delta": "Registration distinguishes nil cancellation from an empty list that is submitted before returning false; normal multiselect minimum does not promise empty confirmation. Normal EXP/item restoration is side/position based with explicit partial-write exceptions; loaded OHKO eligibility and caller-side draw-clause semantics are preserved.",
      "B16_action": "Preserve exact facility selection/cancellation boundary in WP65/WP66 party interfaces; do not infer successful empty normal selection, identity-based restore, or exception rollback. Only real touched UI caller clauses require refresh."
    },
    {
      "path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp56-palace-and-arena-variants.md",
      "published_document_delta": "Arena normal sequential replacement retains mind/skill accumulators, opening HP baseline, turn count and cleared start marker. Count at least 3 can judge on turns 3/4/5; body score can exceed 100. Palace unchanged qualified branches remain.",
      "B16_action": "Preserve Arena no-manual-switch versus automatic sequential replacement and current facility presentation boundary. No new B16 source execution or full re-review of Palace required."
    },
    {
      "path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp58-battle-recording-and-playback.md",
      "published_document_delta": "Switch records include legal attack-phase owner-selected substitutes and pre-first-command entry exit scans. Random forced substitutes, deferred end-of-round replacement, unreachable facility switch-style confirmation and Arena sequential replacement are distinguished. Cancellation can append a negative value after EJECTPACK consumption without successful replacement; Arena playback retains counters.",
      "B16_action": "Do not infer that every party selection is random, end-of-round only, or atomic. Align only the actual affected party/menu/caller boundary and retain global playback limits."
    },
    {
      "path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/creature-rpg-wp35-36-57-64-68.md",
      "published_document_delta": "FC-10 now explicitly preserves direct exchanged object identity/default owner and distinguishes in-progress count +1/immediate active-team submission from non-progress registration-only update.",
      "B16_action": "Keep FC-10 other-owner row unchanged; preserve transfer/cancel/retained-item UI evidence without claiming copy or owner rewrite."
    }
  ],
